  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Futures: Integrating Seed Sovereignty and Climate Justice into Zimbabwe&apos;s Frameworks</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will leverage on Silveira House&#x2019;s work in the Citizen Agency for Transformed Food Systems in Zimbabwe (ZIM708) and PRFT&#x2019;s Agriculture Sector Small Grains Producers Focused Policy Analysis by capitalizing on the low-hanging opportunities for influencing the agriculture terrain in the country. The project shall have a national focus that will aim to influence national policies on agroecology, seed sovereignty, and climate justice. The Project will ride on Silveira House&#x2019;s community presence in Mutoko District (Mashonaland East Province) to draw on community voices, experiences, and change stories to influence policy at the national level. It is aimed at promoting the integration of sustainable food systems principles (agroecology, seed sovereignty, and climate justice) into national policy frameworks and budgetary processes for increased government commitment and funding towards these priorities by 2025</narrative>
  </description>
